Suppress spurious FPEs seen with some Eigen versions.

We had in a couple places m_iwidth = 1 / m_width, where the variables
are vectors.  If DIM=3, this is vectorized as two division instruction,
each handing two doubles.  But that means that the second lane of the
second division is reading uninitialized memory.  The result is never used,
so this wouldn't be a problem, except that it can cause FPEs.
